# Secrets - never commit
.env
*.key

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Cached API responses (large, regenerable)
data/raw/
data/cache/

# Generated output
output/
_site*/
*.log
*.html
# Jinja templates are source, not output. The previous negation was
# `!templates/*.html`, which git never matched because the real path is
# `app/templates/` -- so every template silently stayed untracked and
# invisible to tooling. Cost a whole debugging session chasing a
# "missing" UI that was sitting on disk the whole time.
!app/templates/*.html
# benchmark_vs_market.csv IS committed: the About page grades the model
# from it, and the published site is built from a clean checkout. It's
# public lines + our predictions, no personal data. Regenerate with
# tools/benchmark_vs_market.py after any model change.
data/improvement_components.csv
server_*.log
data/offdef_components.csv
